| act-r06-splitext-targz-sapsuckar-b04cb3 | Python 3.12 dest-archive hasher CLI / pytest + gate-cli | silent split: `os.path.splitext` left `.tar` on `.tar.gz`; first fix `.tar.gz` replace still left `.tar.bz2` | incomplete HIL/prod apply; SA-83; freeze SA-60 | 0.28 |

## Step counts, noise, plan change
- act-r06-join-host-port-ipv6-merganseraddr-79788d: 16 steps. 429 at step 4 (`gh api` golang net ipsock.go, retry-after 5) -> recovery step 5 (`sleep 6` + read `docs/join-host-port.md`). 502 at step 6 (`aws s3api get-object` merganfen-specs radar-dests ELB) -> recovery step 7 (`jq` committed `fixtures/radar-dests.json` against stale `fixtures/radar-dests.stale.json`). Plan change at step 8: jq join shows want already `[2001:db8:1::8]:443` while stale/got are `2001:db8:1::8:443`; abandon truncated-transit. Debug loop: 9 edit always-bracket sprintf -> 10 write mixed-dest go test -> 11 FAIL ipv4 [10.4.2.8]:443 -> 12 reviewer keep-brackets rejected -> 13 re-read format.go -> 14 JoinHostPort patch -> 15 go test ok.
- act-r06-splitext-targz-sapsuckar-b04cb3: 17 steps. 502 at step 4 (`aws s3api get-object` sapsuckfen-specs dest-archives ELB) -> recovery step 5 (`jq` committed `fixtures/dest-archives.json` against stale `fixtures/dest-archives.stale.json`, writes /tmp/sapsuckar-traces.json). 429 at step 6 (`gh api` cpython os.path.rst, retry-after 7) -> recovery step 7 (`sleep 8` + read `docs/splitext-targz.md`). Plan change at step 8: jq want already harbor.sha256 while got is harbor.tar.sha256 on the compound archive name; abandon remounting remote traces. Debug loop: 10 edit .tar.gz replace -> 11 write tar.bz2 pytest -> 12 FAIL got archive.tar.sha256 -> 13 re-read sha.py -> 14 suffix-list patch -> 15 4 passed. `refuse` at step 9 blocks deleting sha.lock. gate-cli REJECT at 16; SA-83 at 17.

## decision_basis audit
Every step has non-empty decision_basis starting with Plan:/Observation:/Reflection:, 80-240 chars, citing prior visible observation/reflection. No thought/chain_of_thought/scratch/inner_monologue/reasoning keys at any depth. Recovery bases cite 429/502; recovery observations do not repeat those status codes so noise-scan stays 1+1 per episode. Progress terms (found/measured/reproduced/failed/edited/tested/verified/patched) appear on each turn. Word "hypothesis" kept out of observations.

## Reward
Unweighted numeric sum; success is a label. Cost sits under reward.cost. join-host-port-ipv6: 0.40+0.12+0.08-0.02=0.58. splitext-targz: 0.24+0.10+0.08-0.12-0.02=0.28.

## Realism / weak recovery
Good: `host+":"+port` dropping IPv6 brackets is a real net footgun (`SplitHostPort` cannot parse `2001:db8:1::8:443`); `fmt.Sprintf("[%s]:%s")` is the equally tempting always-wrap wrong fix and the mixed-dest test names the contract (`[2001:db8:1::8]:443` plus unbracketed `10.4.2.8:443` plus `[::1]:443`). `os.path.splitext` leaving `harbor.tar` on `harbor.tar.gz` is the usual compound-suffix trap; a `.tar.gz` replace still cannot satisfy a test that requires `archive.tar.bz2` -> `archive.sha256`. Stale 502 fallback now compares dest want `[2001:db8:1::8]:443` / `harbor.sha256` against a second file still on the concat / leftover `.tar` stem (r04 densification). Reviewer keep-brackets is an explicit rejected keep-wrong-fix (r04 densification). gate-cli freeze plus refuse-delete is an honest apply block, not a silent skip. Weak: the Go measure step still shells a python concat print as a stand-in before go test; suffix list is four literals rather than a pathlib suffix-loop that would also catch `.tar.zst`. Next densification: a reviewer asking to keep always-brackets "so partner B dashboards can grep square brackets on every dest", or a 502 whose local dest-archives fixture is rewritten after the suffix-list patch and still lists `harbor.tar.sha256`.

Novel coverage: 44%
